Usage: make [options] [name=value]... [target]...
Options:
  -B, --always-make            every target out of date
  -C dir, --directory=dir      change to dir before reading the makefiles
  -d, --debug                  say what is made and why
  -e, --environment-overrides  the environment over the makefiles
  -f file, --file=file         read file as a makefile
  -i, --ignore-errors          go on past a command that fails
  -j [n], --jobs[=n]           run n commands at once, or any number
  -w, --print-directory        say the directory make is in, and leaving it
  --no-print-directory         do not, not even in a sub-make
  -k, --keep-going             go on with what does not need a failed target
  -o f, --old-file=f           f as old, and never made
  -W f, --what-if=f            f as just changed
  -n, --dry-run                print the commands, run only + ones
  -p, --print-data-base        print the macros and rules
  -q, --question               status 1 if anything is out of date
  -r, --no-builtin-rules       no built-in rules
  -s, --silent                 do not print the commands
  -S, --stop                   stop at the first failure, undoing -k
  -t, --touch                  touch the targets rather than make them
  --help                       this
